{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792397962,"nonce":"5JITDWWFTyNkCG34ydDjjXFvwq4=","title":"Symbols never record where they are defined","message":"Every symbol is created with `SourceLocation::unknown()` (`compiler/src/tast/symbols.rs`, the `create_*` constructors from line ~1026; also `tast/ast_lowering/decls/registration.rs:158`, `decls/classes.rs:942`, `ast_lowering/stdlib.rs:185`), and no code assigns `definition_location` afterwards.\n\nAnything that maps a source position to a symbol therefore finds nothing. The LSP's `FileSymbolIndex::build` (`lsp/src/analysis.rs:29`) indexes symbols by `definition_location`, so its index is always empty. Hover, go-to-definition, signature help, the document outline and semantic tokens all return nothing for that reason.\n\nFix: stamp the declaration's span (the name token, with file id) when TAST lowering creates each class, interface, enum, abstract, typedef, field, method, property, parameter, local, type parameter and enum constructor. Code that compares locations (`ir/mir/resolve/functions.rs:158,185`) must keep working.","files":null}]}